      "writtenOn": "2026-07-20T15:57:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nice catch!\n\nThe refcount we acquire in `intel_pasid_setup_first_level` (`pkvm_get_domain_cache_tag_assign`) stays until the entry is torn down(`pkvm_put_domain_cache_tag_unassign`). So probably keeping the refcount through this function would solve this issue you mentioned? Having the domain refcount elevated through the life time of PASID entry will be taken care of by pkvm_{get,put}_domain_cache_tag_{un}assign? Putting the domain refcount on this function exit would avoid the TOCTOU race. WDYT?",
